According to Ulta Beauty’s MD&A, the roughly $206.6 million increase in merchandise inventories at October 28, 2023 (end of FY2023) was driven primarily by four factors:[1]  
1. $76 million to support higher demand and reflect product cost increases;  
2. $49 million related to the addition of 31 net new stores opened since October 28, 2022;  
3. $43 million for inventory held at the new market fulfillment center in Greer, South Carolina; and  
4. $40 million for new brand launches.  

Source: Ulta Beauty, Form 10-Q for the period ended October 28, 2023 (0001558370-23-019393), “Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows” discussion.
